# The sha256 of Certificate/axioms.lock: the exact axioms this model was last checked against.
# tests/model/run.py compares it with the lock and fails when they differ, so that any change
# to an axiom's statement sends someone back to the harness and MODEL.md before CI is green.
#
# Filled in when the lock was first written (brief 0005, stage 1c, 17 October 2026). When the
# lock changes, bring the model to it as MODEL.md, "Changing the axioms", says, then replace
# the line below with the output of
#     shasum -a 256 Certificate/axioms.lock
# run from the repository root (keep these comment lines).
#
# Renewed on 17 October 2026, when the words of the propositions' statements joined the lock's
# vocabulary: the 87 axioms and the 37 words they reach are unchanged, byte for byte, so
# MODEL.md's account stands as it was.
#
# Renewed on 18 October 2026, when the words of stage 2's companions (brief 0006) joined the
# vocabulary: 30 new words, the definitions and their auxiliary declarations; the 87 axioms
# and every word already locked are unchanged, byte for byte, so MODEL.md's account stands
# as it was.
#
# Renewed on 18 October 2026, when the words of the mixed angles (brief 0011), which only the
# statements of the companions of III.16 and III.31 reach, joined the vocabulary: 16 new
# words, the definitions and what Lean declares for them; the 87 axioms and every word
# already locked are unchanged, byte for byte, so MODEL.md's account stands as it was.
#
# Renewed on 18 October 2026, when the words of stage 3's statements (brief 0006) joined the
# vocabulary: 13 new words, the arcs and segments with the structure's constructor and fields;
# the 87 axioms and every word already locked are unchanged, byte for byte, so MODEL.md's
# account stands as it was.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026, when the rule that every circle has a centre,
# Tacit.exists_centre, joined the axioms by the owner's decision (brief 0008, section 2):
# 88 axioms, the other 87 and every word of the vocabulary unchanged, byte for byte. Its
# law joins laws.toml, search.py and hyperbolic.py, and MODEL.md gains its row and new
# counts, in the same change.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026 for the combined vocabulary of stages 3 and mixed angles:
